name: sim.addObjectToSelection
description: 
luaSynopsis: There are two versions of this function:
inputs (possibly taken/adapted from C-function counterpart. Adjust accordingly):
1. what: indicates what we want to add. Valid values are sim.handle_single (adds just one object), sim.handle_all (adds all objects in the scene), sim.handle_tree (adds the tree with base objectHandle (inclusive)) and sim.handle_chain (adds the chain with tip objectHandle (inclusive))
2. objectHandle: handle of an object. Doesn't have a meaning if "what" is sim.handle_all
outputs (possibly taken/adapted from C-function counterpart. Adjust accordingly):
